# EngineX AI — optional configuration.
#
# The app runs with no configuration at all: briefs and outreach drafts fall back
# to a deterministic template engine, and "Send email" runs in dry-run mode.
# Webhook integrations (Slack, Teams, Make, Zapier) need no env vars — paste the
# webhook URL on the /integrations page.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM — briefs, outreach drafts and the review agent.
# Recommended: the OpenLLM gateway (OpenAI-compatible). Create an account at
# https://openllm.sh, connect a provider, then set:
# OPENLLM_API_KEY=...
# OPENLLM_ENDPOINT=https://api.openllm.sh/v1
#
# Or talk to OpenAI directly:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#
# ENGINEX_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signal sources — where accounts and signals actually come from.
#
# Each source is independent: set the ones you have and leave the rest blank.
# Unconfigured sources are skipped, and the /integrations page shows which ones
# are live. With nothing set, "Dry run" on that page still works against a
# bundled sample feed, and a scheduled run pulls nothing rather than inventing
# data. See the README for the response shape each source expects.
#
# Webz.io News Search — press coverage for funding rounds and leadership moves.
# WEBZ_API_TOKEN=...
# WEBZ_QUERIES=["company raises funding round data platform","company appoints chief data officer"]
# WEBZ_MAX_RESULTS=10            # 50 is the practical ceiling
# WEBZ_BASE_URL=https://api.webz.io

# Generic REST source — any JSON API you have credentials for: job boards, ATS
# feeds, tender portals, people data. Point it at the URL and map the fields
# once. {page} in the URL is replaced per page.
# INGEST_HTTP_URL=https://api.example.com/jobs?company=acme&page={page}
# INGEST_HTTP_TOKEN=...
# INGEST_HTTP_LABEL=Acme job board
# INGEST_HTTP_ITEMS_PATH=data.items                    # default: finds items/results/data/jobs/...
# INGEST_HTTP_FIELD_MAP={"companyName":"company.name","text":"description","url":"link","postedAt":"created_at"}
# INGEST_HTTP_METHOD=GET
# INGEST_HTTP_MAX_PAGES=3

# Sources with no API of their own push candidates to POST /api/ingest instead.
# Set a shared secret to keep that endpoint closed:
# INGEST_SECRET=...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Direct email sending (opt-in).
# Leave unset to keep sends simulated. EngineX does not send by default — the
# report keeps sending/deliverability with a specialised tool.
#
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend            # or postmark, sendgrid
# EMAIL_API_KEY=...
# EMAIL_FROM falls back to the sender address in the service profile.
# EMAIL_BASE_URL=https://api.resend.com
# POSTMARK_STREAM=outbound
